{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1361189-poll-what-canon-dynastic-npc-should-be-the-parents-gardians-to-these-pc-s","id":1361189,"title":"POLL: What canon Dynastic NPC should be the parents & gardians to these PC's?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-15T16:56:41-08:00","id":1361189,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon7.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> POLL: What canon Dynastic NPC should be the parents & gardians to these PC's?","content":"A followup <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1357521-tell-me-about-your-dynasty-s-secondary-schools-games\">to this thread. </a><br /> <br /> I need drama to make this game work. Thus, I need some real Drama Momma's (&amp; Daddies). Oh. &amp; <b>Aunts &amp; Uncles</b>. (Stupid Dynasty &amp; it's stupid insistence on the importance of extended family.)<br /> <br /> <b>The PC's will be Dynastic children going to school.</b> They have not Exalted, yet. (&amp; some of them might not... DRAMA!!!)<br /> <br /> I need to decide who there <b>parents</b> will be <b>&amp;</b> who their <b>primary guardians</b> in their House will be (because most Dynastic children are raised not by their parents, but by other extended members of their House, like Aunts &amp; Uncles.)<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://external-content.duckduckgo.com/iu/?u=http%3A%2F%2F2.bp.blogspot.com%2F-JXENEOH6q1g%2FTZtcTEVHq0I%2FAAAAAAAAAVE%2FTap-GOSdAPc%2Fs1600%2Fare-you-my-mommy-doctor-who_1.jpg&amp;f=1&amp;nofb=1\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> &quot;Are you my Mommy...?&quot;<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://external-content.duckduckgo.com/iu/?u=http%3A%2F%2Fvignette2.wikia.nocookie.net%2Fparody%2Fimages%2F0%2F0a%2FDarth_Vader_with_a_guitar..jpg%2Frevision%2Flatest%2Fscale-to-width-down%2F185%3Fcb%3D20160409091957&amp;f=1&amp;nofb=1\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> &quot;No, but I could adopt you. (My own kids avoid me like the plague...)&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> There are the usual suspects:<br /> <br /> Mnemon (1st Edition- Emperor Palpatine as an eternal 16 yr old girl?) Don't disappoint Mommy, &amp; don't get more powerful/competent then mommy.<br /> Mnemon (2nd Edition, more sane levels of ambition, horrible actions not discussed/optional?) More of a Machiavellian role-model?<br /> Tepet Arada (Am I the only one getting an Uncle Iroh/Obi Won vibe?)<br /> Ragara Myrrun (&quot;Daddy blew up!&quot;)<br /> Peleps Deled (LOL!!! Hard knocks indeed!)<br /> Ragara Bhagwei (Oh boy. Don't ask for relationship advice or the birds &amp; the bees...)<br /> Tepet Ejava (&quot;I will raise you on the battlefield!!!&quot; Who wouldn't want grumpy, distaff/ginger Caesar as their Mom/Aunt?)<br /> Sesus Nagezzer (Speaking about Machiavellian... Also, Jabba the Hut as a parental figure is interesting.)<br /> The Empress, herself (perhaps unknown to anyone as a surprise. You could get a real <i>Great Expectations</i> vibe with this one.)<br /> <br /> Anyone else I forgot who is awesome...<br /> <br /> Want to suggest a Super-KEWL OC's you've made???<br /> <br /> Please feel free to engage in any crack parings. I was entertaining a possible pairing of the Empress &amp; Sesus (forgetting he is her grandson).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4428,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","user":"Daredevil","date":". 01-15-2020, 08:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-15T18:07:36-08:00","id":1361197,"title":"","content":"Given that the notion of the extended family is something that is derived from real-world traditions in real-world places, I don\u2019t think that \u201cstupid\u201d is the appropriate word for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-15T20:26:39-08:00","id":1361206,"title":"","content":"I think they were being sarcastic Alucard. <br /> <br /> As for the few dynast I've made, I try to avoid having a super important dynast as their parents since I figure most players will be jumping onto that train.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14713-chronos12","name":"Chronos12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14713_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-15T21:32:14-08:00","id":1361209,"title":"","content":"Go big or go home, Saibok Guato. Either still alive, somehow, or finding some of his old stuff and realizing a direct family line connection. There's also Berit from What Fire has Wrought, she's got a half a dozen plotlines all her own about making her own house or baking people or what have you. Bal Keraz, the head of the Imperial Treasury could be kind of cool.<br /> <br /> Cynis Cogen could be fun, he's a playboy partyboy drug adventurer turned immaculate monk, he's got a major principle against empty pleasure but a minor one for it as well. He's the uncle that knows better but still can't help but fist bump one of his nieces at some points.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-15T21:55:00-08:00","id":1361215,"title":"","content":"Iirc, most dynastic children are raised by nannies and tutors and schools, not by aunts and uncles. You might call in an Aunt or Uncle if they have some special skills that you want the kid to learn, but I don\u2019t think they\u2019d necessarily have much more contact than the kid\u2019s parents.<br /> <br /> or am I remembering wrong?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-16T04:45:39-08:00","id":1361253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1361189-poll-what-canon-dynastic-npc-should-be-the-parents-gardians-to-these-pc-s?p=1361215#post1361215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Iirc, most dynastic children are raised by nannies and tutors and schools, not by aunts and uncles. You might call in an Aunt or Uncle if they have some special skills that you want the kid to learn, but I don\u2019t think they\u2019d necessarily have much more contact than the kid\u2019s parents.<br /> <br /> or am I remembering wrong?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Second Edition held that dynastic children were <i>always</i> handed over to wet nurses as soon as possible to prevent forming an <i>inappropriate maternal bond</i>, and there after the mother pays little <i>personal </i>attention to her offspring, placing them <i>entirely </i>in the care of mortal tutors and nannies.<br /> <br /> In Third Edition, while such <i>outsourcing </i>of child care still forms the core of dynastic child rearing, the mother is <i>not required</i> to <i>completely</i> distance themselves (though that is not discouraged either). Loving their children is not frowned upon, but spoiling them is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 01-16-2020, 07:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-16T10:54:08-08:00","id":1361300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1361189-poll-what-canon-dynastic-npc-should-be-the-parents-gardians-to-these-pc-s?p=1361215#post1361215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Iirc, most dynastic children are raised by nannies and tutors and schools, not by aunts and uncles. You might call in an Aunt or Uncle if they have some special skills that you want the kid to learn, but I don\u2019t think they\u2019d necessarily have much more contact than the kid\u2019s parents.<br /> <br /> or am I remembering wrong?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh no. Greyman is correct. I am remembering wrong.<br /> <br /> I think I am mis-remembering the latter section in 2nd Ed MoEP:tDB pg 19 &amp; some other section I haven't found yet.<br /> &quot;The average Dynastic household has upward of 100 closely related family members, a dozen or so visiting distant cousins who have yet to strike out on their own, a handful of family friends and 30 to 40 mortals to take care of the cooking, cleaning, tutoring and secretarial matters.&quot;<br /> <br /> Geez. That is intimidating. How am I supposed to cook up so many NPC's? Or a fraction of that number? I'm writing these posts because I am running on creative fumes, here.<br /> <br /> Perhaps I should stick to the misinterpretation? <br /> <br /> Also, I really doubt I'd get much traction with a post asking for Forum Members advice on making interesting nannies &amp; nurses. Only one poster answered the question I asked in this Thread (<b>thank you DrLoveMonkey</b>), &amp; I made it multiple choice with 2 write in options (&amp; DrLoveMonkey does get bonus points for the multiple write ins, btw).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-16T11:27:21-08:00","id":1361309,"title":"","content":"Alfred Pennyworth is a pretty cool Nanny.<br /> As is Mary Poppins/Yondu.<br /> <br /> One of my best 2E games had all the characters be kids of Bhagwei and Banoba. Ragara was the BBEG (well, Ragara and the Ebon Dragon).<br /> <br /> If the question is &quot;which Dynast?&quot; the answer is, basically always &quot;Ragara Bhagwei&quot;.<br /> <br /> Mnemon is also pretty interesting, with plenty of kids. I also really like Berit or V'neef.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-16T13:20:29-08:00","id":1361334,"title":"","content":"Mnemon (3rd Edition): Helicopter matriarch. She <i>will</i> be keeping an eye on your grades and make sure you know if she doesn\u2019t like what she sees.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-16T13:51:42-08:00","id":1361338,"title":"","content":"Do you know what Houses the PCs will be from? If they're V'neef, for example, then V'neef herself may actually be their mum, for example.<br /> Obviously as complex as the Dynasty is, a kid from any house could have Mnemon as paternal grandmother (or great-grandmother,or great-great) but she probably doesn't care much about them if they don't carry her name.<br /> So that would narrow it down a bit.<br /> <br /> I should say, in my experience, letting players choose their own attached NPCs works best (or give them a whole bunch and see which they gravitate to, but that's more work) as they're more invested in the plot lines and character development it drives (ie &quot;My character has a military-obsessed mother but just wants to be an artist&quot;). But that depends on your players: maybe they don't know anything about Exalted NPCs. And also if there's a player who's a massive fanboy/girl about a certain character, they might be upset if your interpretation of the character is different from theirs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-16T17:55:47-08:00","id":1361369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chronos12</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1361189-poll-what-canon-dynastic-npc-should-be-the-parents-gardians-to-these-pc-s?p=1361206#post1361206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the few dynast I've made, I try to avoid having a super important dynast as their parents since I figure most players will be jumping onto that train.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you use more 'low key' canon NPC's or OC's you've made? I'd enjoy hearing more, either way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1361189-poll-what-canon-dynastic-npc-should-be-the-parents-gardians-to-these-pc-s?p=1361209#post1361209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Go big or go home, Saibok Guato. Either still alive, somehow, or finding some of his old stuff and realizing a direct family line connection.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love the bombast here. No. I was pushing it with the Empress suggestion. I shouldn't... I couldn't... Hmmm...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1361189-poll-what-canon-dynastic-npc-should-be-the-parents-gardians-to-these-pc-s?p=1361209#post1361209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also Berit from What Fire has Wrought, she's got a half a dozen plotlines all her own about making her own house or baking people or what have you. Bal Keraz, the head of the Imperial Treasury could be kind of cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are either of them in the earlier Editions? They both sound interesting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1361189-poll-what-canon-dynastic-npc-should-be-the-parents-gardians-to-these-pc-s?p=1361209#post1361209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cynis Cogen could be fun, he's a playboy partyboy drug adventurer turned immaculate monk, he's got a major principle against empty pleasure but a minor one for it as well. He's the uncle that knows better but still can't help but fist bump one of his nieces at some points.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lol! Great ideas all around.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1361189-poll-what-canon-dynastic-npc-should-be-the-parents-gardians-to-these-pc-s?p=1361253#post1361253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Third Edition, while such <i>outsourcing </i>of child care still forms the core of dynastic child rearing, the mother is <i>not required</i> to <i>completely</i> distance themselves (though that is not discouraged either). Loving their children is not frowned upon, but spoiling them is.</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes a lot more sense to me. A parent's paternal instincts are extremely powerful, even with a culture negative against such instincts. This newer angle also allows better RP opportunities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1361189-poll-what-canon-dynastic-npc-should-be-the-parents-gardians-to-these-pc-s?p=1361309#post1361309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alfred Pennyworth is a pretty cool Nanny.<br /> As is Mary Poppins/Yondu.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Alfred Pennyworth is most intriguing.<br /> <br /> How would you stat up Mary Poppins &amp; Yondu?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1361189-poll-what-canon-dynastic-npc-should-be-the-parents-gardians-to-these-pc-s?p=1361309#post1361309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of my best 2E games had all the characters be kids of Bhagwei and Banoba. Ragara was the BBEG (well, Ragara and the Ebon Dragon).</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds fun. Could I hear more?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1361189-poll-what-canon-dynastic-npc-should-be-the-parents-gardians-to-these-pc-s?p=1361309#post1361309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the question is &quot;which Dynast?&quot; the answer is, basically always &quot;Ragara Bhagwei&quot;.<br /> <br /> Mnemon is also pretty interesting, with plenty of kids. I also really like Berit or V'neef.</div> </div> </div> </div>They do have a lot of drama potential. Do any books have additional info on Berit &amp; V'neef?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1361189-poll-what-canon-dynastic-npc-should-be-the-parents-gardians-to-these-pc-s?p=1361334#post1361334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mnemon (3rd Edition): Helicopter matriarch. She <i>will</i> be keeping an eye on your grades and make sure you know if she doesn\u2019t like what she sees.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this direction for the character a lot better than 1st Edition's version of her, which seems to be &quot;Emperor Palpatine meets Pretty in Pink.&quot; I can see her character moving in tis direction by the time of 2nd Edition's Scroll of Exalts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1361189-poll-what-canon-dynastic-npc-should-be-the-parents-gardians-to-these-pc-s?p=1361338#post1361338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you know what Houses the PCs will be from? If they're V'neef, for example, then V'neef herself may actually be their mum, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. I'm hopping deciding who the guardians/parents are will answer the question of what House the PC's are under. They will all be living in one House (in both senses). They might be siblings (non-identical twins, if necessary) just to keep the PC's split up as little as possible, or related by in-law relations &amp; being raised under one roof.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1361189-poll-what-canon-dynastic-npc-should-be-the-parents-gardians-to-these-pc-s?p=1361338#post1361338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I should say, in my experience, letting players choose their own attached NPCs works best (or give them a whole bunch and see which they gravitate to, but that's more work) as they're more invested in the plot lines and character development it drives (ie &quot;My character has a military-obsessed mother but just wants to be an artist&quot;). But that depends on your players: maybe they don't know anything about Exalted NPCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>They know nothing of Exalted. I'm hopping to keep them completely in the dark &amp; have them only know what NPC's tell them, especially, about the Anathema.<br /> <br /> I was going to do pregenerated PC's for their first games, just so they can step in &amp; get a feel for the setting &amp; early system differences. (They have limited experience with D&amp;D, &amp; I do not believ any other experience with other games.)<br /> <br /> But perhaps it would be simpler to show them some of these NPC's &amp; have them collectively pick, getting them invested with an initial decision.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-16T19:37:03-08:00","id":1361380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daredevil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1361189-poll-what-canon-dynastic-npc-should-be-the-parents-gardians-to-these-pc-s?p=1361369#post1361369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you use more 'low key' canon NPC's or OC's you've made? I'd enjoy hearing more, either way.</div> </div> </div> </div>OC's but I would have them be more or less absents for my character.<br /> <br /> Again I tend to assume the either the canon of the major character children is already known or that the other players will likely jump onto it.<br /> <br /> Edit: To be clear I haven't played a Dragonblooded game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":14713,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14713-chronos12","user":"Chronos12","date":". 01-18-2020, 04:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14713-chronos12","name":"Chronos12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14713_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T00:18:11-08:00","id":1361400,"title":"","content":"I'd likely stat up Mary Poppins (or Yondu) as god-blooded. Basically normal people who have neat tricks.<br /> <br /> In my Ragara game the characters (Banoba's twin sons and Bhagwei's daughter) started fresh out of secondary school. They went North, officially to secure House financial assets, unofficially to gather information to cure the Great Contagion, unbeknownst to them to kill a Lunar. Banoba would write to them, Bhagwei would send Infallible Messenger and between them they would try to herd the PCs into plot remotely. Eventually they returned home from the Threshold, somewhat disillusioned about the Dynasty, to find grandfather had a new lease on life (curtousy of finding the Broken Winged Crane, which in this story would be written by his sister in the future). Wedding Band of the Scarlet Bride empowered Ragara took the Throne, appeasing Mnemon with an unparalleled book of sorcery (which she would later use as the basis of the Broken Winged Crane). Banoba uncovered the conspiracy and paid with his life to warn the PCs, and Bhagwei helped the PCs unleash the Great Contagion on the Imperial City (and was last seen holding back an endless horde of demons led by Mara). Game ended with the Imperial City reduced to a shadowland, Mnemon disappeared and the PCs finding Ragara's corpse missing a finger. (Game was then going to progress to the Bull of the North conquering all the allies they'd made in the North, and the Mask of Winters proposing an alliance to win the territory back... but I started playing a three year Pathfinder campaign so it never happened.)<br /> <br /> Whilst staying on the Blessed Isle I had them move to a different cousin's house every session and just winged it with no intention of reusing the same character twice.<br /> <br /> Not a lot of info on Berit beyond WFHW. V'neef (as a house) is in pretty much every book about the Realm/Dragon-Blooded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T00:49:39-08:00","id":1362067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daredevil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1361189-poll-what-canon-dynastic-npc-should-be-the-parents-gardians-to-these-pc-s?p=1361369#post1361369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are either of them in the earlier Editions? They both sound interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure Berit\u2019s new.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I like this direction for the character a lot better than 1st Edition's version of her, which seems to be &amp;quot;Emperor Palpatine meets Pretty in Pink.&amp;quot; I can see her character moving in tis direction by the time of 2nd Edition's Scroll of Exalts. </div> </div> </div>To be clear she\u2019s still ruthless and ambitious enough for the whole empire, but has a more personable side that members of her house (and <i>only</i> members of her house) tend to see lots of in the course of the helicopter matriarching. Which, if you\u2019re looking for a hilarious curveball twist to throw at a player if the chronicle ever skips a few decades, can potentially include offering them a hand-me-down husband (as in from herself).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T14:29:36-08:00","id":1362233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daredevil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1361189-poll-what-canon-dynastic-npc-should-be-the-parents-gardians-to-these-pc-s?p=1361300#post1361300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I am mis-remembering the latter section in 2nd Ed MoEP:tDB pg 19 &amp; some other section I haven't found yet.<br /> &amp;quot;The average Dynastic household has upward of 100 closely related family members, a dozen or so visiting distant cousins who have yet to strike out on their own, a handful of family friends and 30 to 40 mortals to take care of the cooking, cleaning, tutoring and secretarial matters.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Geez. That is intimidating.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll note that is the only part of any of the Editions that described multiple generations living all at once in a single household, and it was contradicted by several other parts of even Second Edition.<br /> <br /> How many children do folks suppose Mnemon has? I imagine somewhere around twenty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T10:56:11-08:00","id":1362462,"title":"","content":"Living or dead? She is hundreds of years old.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T11:40:27-08:00","id":1362473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1361189-poll-what-canon-dynastic-npc-should-be-the-parents-gardians-to-these-pc-s?p=1362462#post1362462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Living or dead?</div> </div> </div> </div>Either or. I should have said &quot;has had&quot;; those twenty include a few mortals who are long gone at the very least.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">She is hundreds of years old.</div> </div> </div> </div>But has probably taken the utmost care to only ever have children every twelve to twenty years.<br /> <br /> Twenty children is surely way extreme for most Dragon Blooded. It's not just that Mnemon has lived longer, but that she's still in a youthful mould and retains certain priorities, where I expect few other Exalted to spend more than a century having kids.<br /> <br /> But keeping in mind how progenitive Essence lends itself to having a lot fewer children than would be technically possible for a four hundred year old woman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T14:33:26-08:00","id":1364034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daredevil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1361189-poll-what-canon-dynastic-npc-should-be-the-parents-gardians-to-these-pc-s#post1361189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Stupid Dynasty &amp; it's stupid insistence on the importance of extended family.)</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, the funny thing is that it looks a lot to me like the importance that the Scarlet Dynasty places in extended family almost completely drowns out and supercedes a sense of identity with or loyalty to nuclear family. You probably stop living with your parents for good past the age of nine, and even their distant authority over you seems to end once you've been married. After that you're just obligated to the general hierarchical network of the House and however it interacts with your particular work assignments.<br /> <br /> Although I imagine that Dynasty etiquette still holds that parents get a distinct form of respectful address; you do owe them that for the work they put into ensuring that you were brought up correctly.<br /> <br /> I definitely think a sense of closeness between siblings is more of the exception. After all, of everything goes to tradition, by the time a sibling is born than you're a qualified adult who's off adventuring in the Threshold or living in the home of some older cousins. You're hardly ever brought up alongside any siblings, is there much basis to feel any more kinship to them than any other Dynasts of the same age? I think that also has implications for any sense of people being aunts or uncles.<br /> <br /> Mind, I think that people throughout House Mnemon feel something closer to being siblings among one another, by virtue of the common experience of the matriarch's input into their own childhoods and general lives thereafter. <br /> <br /> I had this idea that a common feature of Mnemon-exclusive salons is them all fondly reminiscing over times that she was especially stern with them. Maybe they have a little party game in the style of the Yorkshireman where they compete to come up with increasingly outlandish stories about childhood shenanigans that led to her giving them The Look. Mnemon politely pretends to be unaware of such practices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T23:39:29-08:00","id":1364108,"title":"","content":"The thing about the &quot;upward of 100 closely related family members&quot; remark is that, even if taken at face value - what i find pretty debatable (&quot;a dynastic household with more family than servants? preposterous!&quot;) - that number would be more of a soft ceiling than the medium. In my dragon-blooded games, where i did make a point of getting some milleage out of the whole thing, i would have around 10-25 dynasts between elder(s), its adult children and children with wildly varying ages, under the same roof along with a few other relatives in extended visit/mooching off for a number of reasons.<br /> <br /> House staff would be a few talented (skill 3-5) mortal teachers, tutors, nannies &amp; other specialists with the occasional weirdo - god-blood, thaumaturgist, sorcerer, wyld mutant, familiar with speech capacity - mixed in, along with about a dozen to multiple dozens of more general, not specially skilled but serviceably competent (all 2s) mortal servants.<br /> <br /> Well, except for the Sinasi (homebrewed cadet house from my games), that due to their past centuries of &quot;going native&quot; as guerilla fighters/bandit lords in the Scavenger Lands and East, penchant for exotic mounts &amp; sorcery and (loose, quite unofficial &amp; strongly denied) connections to fallen houses like Chanos, Iselsi, Jerah, Manosque and Forest Witches, had a much greater than usual number of spirit, good-blooded or inteligent animals in their retinues, what only made them more backward/outre/scandalous for more &quot;proper&quot; houses. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 01-30-2020, 02:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T00:50:45-08:00","id":1364114,"title":"","content":"I don't think that big extended family is supposed to all be living at the same estate, are they? Maybe like 1-12 on average, I'd imagine. Except maybe their house's section of the Imperial Palace. They'd mostly be scattered over hundreds or thousands of mansions spread all over their provinces, or wintering in lavish appartments in the cities or near government or religious compounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T02:30:44-08:00","id":1364119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1361189-poll-what-canon-dynastic-npc-should-be-the-parents-gardians-to-these-pc-s?p=1364108#post1364108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> its adult children</div> </div> </div> </div>It consistently appears that adulthood is the point at which you're supposed to start making your own way in the world. We <i>do</i> get references to living in somebody else's home before you can afford your own, but that's of a more distant relative than your parents.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> children with wildly varying ages </div> </div> </div>It sounds like there are a lot of leftovers in that mix.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> House staff would be a few talented (skill 3-5) mortal teachers, tutors, nannies &amp; other specialists with the occasional weirdo - god-blood, thaumaturgist, sorcerer, wyld mutant, familiar with speech capacity - mixed in, along with about a dozen to multiple dozens of more general, not specially skilled but serviceably competent (all 2s) mortal servants. </div> </div> </div>With the description of how big those places are, it takes a staff of hundreds just to keep the place clean.<br /> <br /> I agree that it's kind of odd that the household is consistently the main unit of Dynast society but the single time it was ever described in detail was wrong. I also get the impulse to make the household sizable to fit certain kinds of drama despite every detail pushing against it.<br /> <br /> My personal model to try and reconcile those goes thus:<br /> <br /> The core of every household is the woman in charge and her husband. Within it, her word is practically law, his only slightly below it. They may have a child under the age of nine at the time, attended to by a personal staff of nannies and tutors; under exceptional circumstances such as multiple births, adoption of leftover children, they may have more than one.<br /> <br /> Typically there will be a single younger Dynast in residence, just a few years out of graduation and not yet able to sustain a household or married. The relationship is mutually beneficial; the lodger gets not only a roof over their head, but a superior who can provide professional contacts and additional mentorship, plus the odd lavish gift (items to grow one's wardrobe are common), while the other gets a share of the younger's stipend to inject some liquid cash into the house account and an agent for their endeavours with more mobility, plus a bit of extra tutelage for children of present. Sometimes there are two, but supporting that many new Dynasts is a mark of significant wealth and status, and marks the household of one of the family's top people.<br /> <br /> There may also likely be one or two residents of equal, occasionally greater, status than the householders, here on an extended visit (or possibly because their own current fortunes preclude residing in their own place). They'll be peers to the main couple, possibly participants in their plans and schemes, and in the event of children being present are vital to instilling in them an early sense of House identity and values.<br /> <br /> Next are the unExalted Dynasts, usually between five and a dozen. Some unExalted Dynasts can support their own households, maybe even some here will go on to do so if they get good marriages or can make a fortune, but many will reside in the home of an Exalted relative to live in the manner that they grew up accustomed to. They still serve a vital function, having been educated to a level and with sufficient status and loyalties to handle jobs that are a bit low for the Exalted but seen as above or not to be trusted with most patricians.<br /> <br /> Then there are the patricians, who may have significant numbers. Some are people who run important aspects of the household's business, but most are live in members of the Dynasts' assorted entourages (which can include even the mortal ones), here to provide companionship and maybe not exactly earning money to support their own home. They're in the same position as the royal post of lady-in-waiting or the make equivalent I presume existed but don't know the name of off-hand.<br /> <br /> And beneath them are the staff, the free servants and slaves, often managed by one of the more high-born levels of peasant who typically reports to a patrician or unExalted intermediary but in some cases is respected and accomplished enough to have direct contact with the lady of the house.<br /> <br /> On the face of it, the internal hierarchy of the household should seem obvious, but interluding Exalted might find that mortals who have been around for a lot longer can exert a bit more standing, especially if they mask it with insinuations and a catty attitude. Even servants can get in on that, if they know the views of the head couple are a tad negative.<br /> <br /> Things are a bit different in the headquarters of each Great House, those are usually a few households mixed together under the matriarch. Especially in House Mnemon; she likes to invite other households with children for extended stays.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T04:03:06-08:00","id":1364128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1361189-poll-what-canon-dynastic-npc-should-be-the-parents-gardians-to-these-pc-s?p=1364119#post1364119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It consistently appears that adulthood is the point at which you're supposed to start making your own way in the world. We <i>do</i> get references to living in somebody else's home before you can afford your own, but that's of a more distant relative than your parents.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but there's always a balance between societal &quot;ideal&quot; expectations and actual realities. A dynast couple might insist on their unmarried child(ren) staying with them because their manse is in the Imperial City and that's where <b>real </b>action and social circuit (the better to find prospective mates) are. A just married son or daughter has a strong personal &amp;/or professional relationship and some attachment to their parent for a number of reasons practical or emotional and the house has more than enough room for them and their children (not to mention the elder enjoys the hustle family brings to the house and ocasionally playing the doting grandparent). Or some child, married or not, feels a little (too) possessive and is bothered with the idea of letting their parent's new mortal partner &amp; children taking too many liberties in managing the house of their infancy. And so on, among motives big &amp; petty. It's family, excuses will abound if one just thinks a bit on it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1361189-poll-what-canon-dynastic-npc-should-be-the-parents-gardians-to-these-pc-s?p=1364119#post1364119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It sounds like there are a lot of leftovers in that mix.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on what one defines as leftovers - it's good to remember that even &quot;young senator of the Realm&quot; Nellens Poramo, under the youthful face is a man in his 60s that could just as well be a PC's dad or grandad. Ledaal Kes while having the face of someone between late teens to early twenties is actually about 140 years much like his wife Ragara Szaya.<br /> <br /> That and the gaps between children - that depending on individual dynast couple can vary from anything between 5 to 25 or 50 years - can result in some weirdly slanted family set ups depending on the age of matriarch or patriarch involved. A child of Szaya and Kes <i>could be the uncle or aunt of an exalt its elder by a whole century</i> with children &amp; grandchildren of their own, and they are far from old by the standards of the Realm. Things can only get weirder depending on details like who exalts or not, which ones marry other dragon-blooded or mortals (what may or not lead to a couple having shorter gaps between children, depeding on their actual level of partnership &amp; intimacy) and so on.<br /> <br /> And now i'm remembering occasionally messing a group of PCs with a pair of loving/pestering cousins, that looked uncanilly like each other beside an difference of about 140 years. And then one of the PCs decided to mess <b>other </b>dynasts by taking either to social events while being completely vague and dubious about which one. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Or a Mnemon PC of mine that would occasionally fllirt/spar with a single cousin.... that fought alongside Arada in the Jochim campaign. Dynastic social dynamics can get quite funky at times. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 01-30-2020, 07:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T06:05:27-08:00","id":1364143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1361189-poll-what-canon-dynastic-npc-should-be-the-parents-gardians-to-these-pc-s?p=1364128#post1364128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, but there's always a balance between societal &quot;ideal&quot; expectations and actual realities. A dynast couple might insist on their unmarried child(ren) staying with them because their manse is in the Imperial City and that's where <b>real </b>action and social circuit (the better to find prospective mates) are. A just married son or daughter has a strong personal &amp;/or professional relationship and some attachment to their parent for a number of reasons practical or emotional and the house has more than enough room for them and their children (not to mention the elder enjoys the hustle family brings to the house and ocasionally playing the doting grandparent). Or some child, married or not, feels a little (too) possessive and is bothered with the idea of letting their parent's new mortal partner &amp; children taking too many liberties in managing the house of their infancy. And so on, among motives big &amp; petty. It's family, excuses will abound if one just thinks a bit on it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>So... not the norm. Fine, so long as that is clear.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Depends on what one defines as leftovers </div> </div> </div>Leftover children: the pejorative term in the Scarlet Dynasty for a child born before the parents took the twelve to twenty years necessary to rejuvenate their progenitive Essence, dramatically decreasing their odds of Exaltation (as well as being erroneously believed to weaken their bloodline).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> it's good to remember that even &quot;young senator of the Realm&quot; Nellens Poramo, under the youthful face is a man in his 60s that could just as well be a PC's dad or grandad. Ledaal Kes while having the face of someone between late teens to early twenties is actually about 140 years much like his wife Ragara Szaya. </div> </div> </div>When you draw a distinction between adult children and children of varying ages, I presume the latter refers specifically to people below the age of eighteen to twenty.<br /> <br /> If you've got several people below that age with differing numbers in the house, I can buy that they're being home-schooled, but they still have to deal with that whole thing of &quot;sorry Timmy, mammy and daddy couldn't restrain themselves for long enough, so no Exaltation for you&quot;.<br /> <br /> Hmm, suddenly I'm thinking that the one social allowance made for leftover children is the right to not address their parents with respectful monikers once they reach adulthood; their lack of decorum has done you wrong, and you're permitted to share in the general House disdain for them.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I... wasn't really paying attention to the implication that you were describing the layout of Dynast households in past games, so it seems like a lot of what I'm referring to is not worth minding.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't personally agree with putting so many Dynasts together in a single household even back then, but that's a minor difference in taste and opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 01-30-2020, 09:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T07:53:11-08:00","id":1364157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1361189-poll-what-canon-dynastic-npc-should-be-the-parents-gardians-to-these-pc-s?p=1364119#post1364119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It consistently appears that adulthood is the point at which you're supposed to start making your own way in the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you let me know what in the 3e text actually indicates or implies that children are actively expected to start their own households, rather than attaching themselves long-term to an existing household? The benefits of the latter are significant, both in terms of reduced financial burden for those involved and the ability to more easily draw on one another's connections, talents, and other resources.<br /> <br /> (The dynamics of larger households is something we should have addressed in <i>What Fire Has Wrought</i> or <i>The Realm</i>, but there was so much to cover that it slipped past.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T10:25:31-08:00","id":1364186,"title":"","content":"With the caveat that I absolutely disageee with with Isator's reading (in my game there are at least 11 adult Dragon-Blooded in the Mnemon Alinos household -- I picture closer to three dozen but only 11 willing to uproot to the Threshold on a fool's errand), the text does say:<br /> <br /> &quot;When an unmarried Dynast stays in one place, she\u2019s rarely on her own. Instead, it\u2019s normal for her to attach herself to an existing household&quot;<br /> <br /> Which <i>kinda</i> implies that it's singletons who attach and married couples (&quot;real&quot; adults) start their own household.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 01-31-2020, 03:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T11:01:14-08:00","id":1364194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1361189-poll-what-canon-dynastic-npc-should-be-the-parents-gardians-to-these-pc-s?p=1364186#post1364186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the caveat that I absolutely disageee with with Isator's reading (in my game there are at least 11 adult Dragon-Blooded in the Mnemon Alinos household -- I picture closer to three dozen but only 11 willing to uproot to the Threshold on a fool's errand), the text does say:<br /> <br /> &quot;When an unmarried Dynast stays in one place, she\u2019s<br /> rarely on her own. Instead, it\u2019s normal for her to attach herself to an existing household&quot;<br /> <br /> Which <i>kinda</i> implies that it's singletons who attach and married couples (&quot;real&quot; adults) start their own household.</div> </div> </div> </div>This section specifically talks about what unmarried Dynasts do before marriage, and wasn't intended to differentiate their behavior from that of married Dynasts. Still, having paged through the material just now, it's clear that we failed to supply any useful information on the topic. Short of finding word count to detail a large Dynastic household in some future book and explicitly indicating that it's indicative of broader Dynastic trends, there's not much to be done about it at this stage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T11:04:24-08:00","id":1364195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1361189-poll-what-canon-dynastic-npc-should-be-the-parents-gardians-to-these-pc-s?p=1364157#post1364157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you let me know what in the 3e text actually indicates or implies that children are actively expected to start their own households</div> </div> </div> </div>That is not what I said.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">rather than attaching themselves long-term to an existing household? The benefits of the latter are significant, both in terms of reduced financial burden for those involved and the ability to more easily draw on one another's connections, talents, and other resources.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a thing I made multiple references to.<br /> <br /> EDIT: A significant concern for me in how I imagine this subject is that there are only ten thousand Exalted Dynasts, and the Blessed Isle is huge.<br /> <br /> If a Great House is expected to consist of around 100 people, it creates an impression that each Great House lives in about ten mansions. While engaged with government over and business in a territory larger than Qing China.<br /> <br /> I can accept some degree of fudging, but that's much too far.<br /> <br /> Although sure, it's hard to always be sure exactly how many references to Dynasts are meant to be referring to the Exalted. I did ask a question in the relevant thread about ideas for the ratio of mortal to Exalted in a given House, but it was overlooked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 01-30-2020, 02:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T12:00:09-08:00","id":1364201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1361189-poll-what-canon-dynastic-npc-should-be-the-parents-gardians-to-these-pc-s?p=1364195#post1364195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is not what I said.</div> </div> </div> </div>I apologize.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1361189-poll-what-canon-dynastic-npc-should-be-the-parents-gardians-to-these-pc-s?p=1364195#post1364195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: A significant concern for me in how I imagine this subject is that there are only ten thousand Exalted Dynasts, and the Blessed Isle is huge.<br /> <br /> If a Great House is expected to consist of around 100 people,</div> </div> </div> </div>The Great Houses average a thousand Dragon-Blooded apiece, not a hundred.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I think you mean a household of 100 people? I doubt any single household would have anywhere near that many part-time occupants, let alone full-time occupants.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1361189-poll-what-canon-dynastic-npc-should-be-the-parents-gardians-to-these-pc-s?p=1364195#post1364195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it creates an impression that each Great House lives in about ten mansions. While engaged with government over and business in a territory larger than Qing China.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a wide range of potential living arrangements, from &quot;alone in a townhouse&quot; to &quot;married couple just setting up their own household&quot; to &quot;married couple plus half a dozen assorted younger siblings, cousins, and grown children&quot; to &quot;twenty-odd Dynasts cohabiting in a Gormenghastian mansion.&quot; I'm in no way trying to imply that <i>every</i> Dynast immediately jumps permanently into a hamster pile with their relatives. I'm just saying that it's not the reverse; going off to build a villa just for two isn't the assumed default.<br /> <br /> Larger assemblies would be in places where those Dynasts have something to do, typically in or near major cities. There would also be a significant amount of transience; if you hold a ministerial post in a city a few days' travel from the household estate, you might have an apartment at the former and a suite at the latter, traveling back and forth as needed.<br /> <br /> Dynasts who have cause to live in isolated backwaters wouldn't be in a giant mansion full of Dynasts because there wouldn't be enough going on there to fill such a place up. They may just rent a townhouse, with the intent of moving on later to someplace worth putting down roots. (A married Dynast may end up living apart from their spouse this way, visiting only often enough to have children and to attend the most important social functions.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1361189-poll-what-canon-dynastic-npc-should-be-the-parents-gardians-to-these-pc-s?p=1364195#post1364195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although sure, it's hard to always be sure exactly how many references to Dynasts are meant to be referring to the Exalted. I did ask a question in the relevant thread about ideas for the ratio of mortal to Exalted in a given House, but it was overlooked.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to assume that it's roughly fifty-fifty overall, though varying from house to house and household to household, but the text as written should function well enough if you shift the proportions around to your taste. The text wasn't written with the intent of a specific ratio, just a very broad order-of-magnitude parity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T17:36:22-08:00","id":1364254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1361189-poll-what-canon-dynastic-npc-should-be-the-parents-gardians-to-these-pc-s?p=1364201#post1364201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: I think you mean a household of 100 people? I doubt any single household would have anywhere near that many part-time occupants, let alone full-time occupants.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. I know that's an extreme that hasn't quite been brought up here, but that passage from Manual: Dragon Blooded left a strong impression on me.<br /> <br /> I read the Second Edition Core's description of the home life of Dynasts first and that in the Manual second, and I've been spending a long time fleeing from the latter in pursuit of the former.<br /> <br /> I'm already focusing on a past thing I dislike more than is fitting to my resolution, I'm going to leave that alone now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a wide range of potential living arrangements, from &amp;quot;alone in a townhouse&amp;quot; to &amp;quot;married couple just setting up their own household&amp;quot; to &amp;quot;married couple plus half a dozen assorted younger siblings, cousins, and grown children&amp;quot; to &amp;quot;twenty-odd Dynasts cohabiting in a Gormenghastian mansion.&amp;quot; I'm in no way trying to imply that <i>every</i> Dynast immediately jumps permanently into a hamster pile with their relatives. I'm just saying that it's not the reverse; going off to build a villa just for two isn't the assumed default.<br /> <br /> Larger assemblies would be in places where those Dynasts have something to do, typically in or near major cities. There would also be a significant amount of transience; if you hold a ministerial post in a city a few days' travel from the household estate, you might have an apartment at the former and a suite at the latter, traveling back and forth as needed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can meet up with that. The versatility it would offer looks valuable to me.<br /> <br /> I'll admit there are some possibilities to the larger end that make for stories I see holding an attraction to me, even if there have been conflicting impulses that took priority.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dynasts who have cause to live in isolated backwaters wouldn't be in a giant mansion full of Dynasts because there wouldn't be enough going on there to fill such a place up. They may just rent a townhouse, with the intent of moving on later to someplace worth putting down roots. (A married Dynast may end up living apart from their spouse this way, visiting only often enough to have children and to attend the most important social functions.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I kept thinking about the image of Medieval nobles moving their entire household between their castles and manors, leaving them otherwise almost completely unoccupied, but I guess this is part of what one gets when the economics of the Scarlet Dynasty are, among other things, not deeply invested in agrarian rents.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to assume that it's roughly fifty-fifty overall, though varying from house to house and household to household, but the text as written should function well enough if you shift the proportions around to your taste. The text wasn't written with the intent of a specific ratio, just a very broad order-of-magnitude parity.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I was looking back on some of What Fire Has Wrought, it did occur to me that it would be a significant thing to differing standards of maximizing the House breeding. Plus some considerations for how many high ranking mortals they think the businesses need to be kept running.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry for being a bit salty; impending Brexit has my mood down. I expect it to pass on a few days.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T03:30:14-08:00","id":1367186,"title":"","content":"Hey, so considering the range in personalities for Dynast characters against the stated standards for how they're supposed to interact with their children, does anybody else think that parents get really nervous about those interactions when their kids aren't looking?<br /> <br /> I'm basing this on an assumption that early childhood consists of things like an extremely formal meeting with one or both of your parents every few weeks, in which they sternly but dispassionately question the child on their progress, have them recite particular pieces, maybe a demonstration of some physical practice, and then dismiss them with neither praise not criticism (that's for the tutors to relay). And it brought me to this image that before and after the meeting the parents would be extremely anxious about the whole thing on grounds such as having to repress their natural personally, being deeply concerned about making the proper impression and being able to effectively review their child's education, and general feeling that they don't know what to make of then because there's no relationship there.<br /> <br /> Heh, suddenly I'm imagining that when V'neef was pregnant for the first time, Mnemon made regular visits to her in which she made subtle insinuations that her charming and outgoing personality was exactly the kind of thing that could mess a child up and she needed to work extra hard to keep it in check. Very nervous around her first few children was V'neef.<br /> <br /> She'd never admit it*, but she modelled the persona she adopted for interacting with the children of of Mnemon's public appearance. Would spend long stretches in front of the mirror trying to get the cadence and expression down pat.<br /> <br /> * Although her oldest children have had enough interactions with their aunty to make an accurate guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T10:53:25-08:00","id":1368327,"title":"","content":"As an important (yet underplayed) plot point in my game (Dynasty of Dovak), Mnemon Danireya went completely off the rails raising her kids as part of her backstory. In Exalted defiance of Realm convention she devoted herself to raising her children personally.<br /> <br /> But yes, I can imagine Dynastic fathers pacing back and forth with worry as their wives (secretly every bit as worried) scold them for getting over emotional about the simple act of proper child rearing right before they see their child for the first time in a week.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T09:52:23-08:00","id":1368957,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4428_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4428\" data-vbnamecard=\"4428\">Daredevil</a> who did you go with in the end?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T18:01:19-07:00","id":1374263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1361189-poll-what-canon-dynastic-npc-should-be-the-parents-gardians-to-these-pc-s?p=1368957#post1368957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4428_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4428\" data-vbnamecard=\"4428\">Daredevil</a> who did you go with in the end?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for following up with me on this topic. I want you to know your posts have been monstrously helpful &amp; a joy to read. I apologize for my sporadic responses.<br /> <br /> The game keeps getting pushed back do to the Player's crazy schedules. (I can't believe how many extracurricular activities their schools have them do. They are literally at the school until <i>9pm</i>. It's very different from when I was in school.)<br /> <br /> When I get to run this thing, I think I will allow them to vote who their Mummy &amp; Daddy will be. They can debate it among themselves &amp; weigh it out. I'll give them a brief overview of the NPC's &amp; what kind of stories &amp; themes they might generate.<br /> <br /> I am a bit torn, myself, between Tepet Ejava or Mnemon as mother, with Sesus Nagezzer or Ragara Myrrun as Daddy, but I don't get a vote. Lattly I really love the idea of Ejava &amp; Myrrun, with Myrrun having the children act as a distraction from his obsessive MA Training. I would get a change to allow the PC's to save Myrrun from exploding, or perhaps help him find a way to transcend DB limitations on SMA Training. The idea of Ejava trying to rebuild her house with her Children is also very powerful.<br /> <br /> I'm planing on using pre-generated Character Sheets initially to get the game going, so I'm hoping this choice will give them a feeling of ownership &amp; investment in their PC's. They seem to like the &quot;Harry Potter meets Game of Thrones&quot; comparisons I've made.<br /> <br /> I'm hoping to compare the different houses to the families in those series, especially the houses in Game of Thrones/Song of Fire &amp; Ice.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4428,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","user":"Daredevil","date":". 03-11-2020, 09:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}